CRASH-06: make sstrcat() check the room left before each write

sstrcat() stopped appending only when offset reached destsize - 1 after a
write. When dest already held destsize - 1 characters, the first write took
offset past that value, the check never matched, and the whole of src and
its terminator were written beyond the buffer. project_readOption() reaches
this with a SWEEP_START/SWEEP_END value of 24 or more characters
(sstrncpy(strDate, s2, 24) then sstrcat(strDate, "/1947", 25)). Test the
bound before writing; results are unchanged whenever there is room.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CRASH-06_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/swmm5.c b/src/legacy/engine/swmm5.c
index 4096c9a..d905790 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/swmm5.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/swmm5.c
@@ -3487,14 +3487,13 @@ size_t sstrcat(char *dest, const char *src, size_t destsize)
 
     // append src
     src_index = 0;
-    while (*(src + src_index) != '\0')
+    // don't copy more than size - dest_len - 1 characters
+    // (checked before each write so that a full dest gets nothing)
+    while (*(src + src_index) != '\0' && offset < destsize - 1)
     {
         *(dest + offset) = *(src + src_index);
         offset++;
         src_index++;
-        // don't copy more than size - dest_len - 1 characters
-        if (offset == destsize - 1)
-            break;
     }
     *(dest + offset) = '\0';
     return strlen(dest);
